'''5.''' To contrive, fabricate, or construct with design or elaborate care: as, to ''weave'' a plot.
{{smaller block|For answer . . . Accaius ''weaveth'' out a long history of things that happened in the persecution under Decius, and of men which to save life forsook faith.
{{right|''Hooker'', Eccles. Polity, vi. 6.}}}}
{{smaller block|<poem>My brain, more busy than the labouring spider,
''Weaves'' tedious snares to trap mine enemies.</poem>
{{right|''Shak.'', 2 Hen. VI., iii. 1. 340.}}}}

'''Wove paper.''' {{smaller|See ''paper''.}}

'''II.''' ''intrans.'' '''1.''' To practise weaving; work with a loom.

