called ''yellow-crowned weaver'' and ''Ploceus icterocephalus.'' This is 7 inches long, of an olive and golden-yellow and black color; it builds a large bottle-shaped or kidney-formed pensile nest. ''Foudia'' is a Madagascar type. The most extensive genus of all is the African ''Hyphantornis,'' with over 30 species, or the golden weavers, as ''H. galbula.'' These birds represent in Africa, or may be compared with, the hang-nest orioles of America. One of the longest- and best-known is ''H. cucullatus'' of western Af-

